===== 6. the width surface was picked in code, and no round cites the open question =====
-- Q9's options, which is what was picked from:
options = [
  "Keyed on const generics directly with a per-width bridge, one row per written width.",
  "A raw nat surface with no const bridge, the consumer spelling the width as a hand-written binary digit tower.",
  "A nat surface with a shipped alias layer, names shipped for the towers.",
  "A nat surface with a consumer-side declaration macro minting the names it wants.",
  "A hybrid: a consumer-facing type alias carries the const parameter, the numeral is keyed on nats, and the bridge fires once at the alias so the algebra never re-enters it.",
  "The width type visible to a consumer is the literal itself, with the structural nat demoted to a hidden projection.",
  "Declare the output width explicitly and check it is wide enough by a free type-level comparison, so no reverse table exists because no output is ever named computationally.",
]
